Z||000000||whamel||09-05-2000||09:14 AM||||     I was changing out my spark plugs on my GT this weekend and one of my wires came apart in my hand. (ARGH!)  I have a couple spares for my '84 and they seemed to be the right length for the job.  I hesitated to substitute them while I wait for my wire order to come in though until I asked here, but is there any functional difference between the plug wires (factory) from the V-6 and the I4?  I didn't think it would actually hurt anything to run them like this for a while (they said it would take a week to fill the order), but I really don't feel like rebuilding another smoked Fiero!  Any input?<BR>Thanks,<BR>Wade<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||StuGood||09-05-2000||12:57 PM||||I'd go ahead and do it.  I don't think the car will know any difference.<P>Aren't you glad you found out about the bad wire when you did, instead of on the road somewhere  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ! ||||reg||14
